            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.2 Revisiting Arithmetic Expressions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.483,
            0.849,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We learnt to write expressions as sums of terms and it became easy for us to read arithmetic expressions. Many times they could have been read in multiple ways and it was confusing. We used "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "swapping",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (adding two numbers in any order) and "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "grouping",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (adding numbers by grouping them conveniently) to find easy ways of evaluating expressions. Swapping and grouping terms does not change the value of the expression. We also learnt to use brackets in expressions, including brackets with a negative sign outside. We learnt the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "distributive property",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (multiple of a sum is the same as sum of multiples)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.65,
            0.848,
            0.687
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us revise these concepts and find the values of the following expressions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.691,
            0.37,
            0.711
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "1. \\quad 23 - 10 \\times 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.715,
            0.379,
            0.734
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "3. \\quad 34 \\ne 14 + 20"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.515,
            0.69,
            0.729,
            0.759
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}&2.\\quad & 83 + 28 - 13 + 32 \\\\&4.\\quad & 42 + 15 - (8 - 7) \\\\&6.\\quad & 7 \\times 4 + 9 \\times 6\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.739,
            0.392,
            0.759
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "68 - (18 + 13)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.763,
            0.415,
            0.783
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "20 \\div 8 \\times (16 - 6)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.788,
            0.848,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us evaluate the first expression, 23 – 10 × 2. First we shall write the terms of the expression. Notice that one of the terms is a number, while the other one has to be converted to a number before adding the two terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.309,
            0.867,
            0.69,
            0.886
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "23-10\\times 2=23+-10\\times 2=23+-20=3"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
